attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 1, `yghU` to `gss`, are carried by 95 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.2% of calls {S1}. The model names 99 to 100% of them, fewest at column 1, `gss`, 99% {S1}.

@variable **A fork opens at column 2**, `pitB`, carried by 76%, with an IS1 family transposase at 38% {S2.c2}. Then columns 4 to 36 are variable, [[glycolate oxidase]] at columns 16 to 22 and [[type II secretion, minor pseudopilins]] at columns 25 to 35 {S2.c4-36, Q}. A branch of 4 shell families runs through columns 44 to 47, [[polysaccharide export]], 22 to 23% {S2.b44}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 99.7 against 83%, and hesitates less there, 0.14 against 0.79 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 2, `pitB`, a fork column, 1.93 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 72 to 79, `cmtA` to `mscS`, are carried by 44 to 36% of chromosomes {S2.c72-79}. The last column is `mscS`, in 36% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 83% of genes**, 0.77 bits on average, perplexity 2.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.16 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 75% against 96% {C}.

